# Secret environment for the reference-delivery example.
#
# Copy to `secrets/.env` (gitignored) only if you need to override a secret by
# env. For the default auth (ChatGPT OAuth) you typically need NOTHING here.
#
# ============================================================================
# Auth option 1 (PREFERRED, DEFAULT): ChatGPT (OpenAI Codex) OAuth subscription
# ============================================================================
# A flat ChatGPT subscription with NO per-call cost. There is NO secret file in
# this repo for it: log in ONCE with the pi CLI to populate the shared auth
# file, which the workers read in place:
#
#     pi /login openai-codex
#
# That writes ~/.pi/agent/auth.json (the path config/temper.env's
# TEMPER_AGENTS_AUTH_FILE points at by default). Nothing to set here.
#
# ============================================================================
# Auth option 2 (OPT-IN): Anthropic OAuth subscription
# ============================================================================
# Switch to Anthropic OAuth by setting this in config/temper.env:
#
#     TEMPER_AGENTS_AUTH=anthropic-oauth
#
# then log in once:
#
#     pi /login anthropic
#
# This uses the same shared auth file (TEMPER_AGENTS_AUTH_FILE). You can set
# TEMPER_AGENTS_ANTHROPIC_MODEL in config/temper.env to override the default.
# Nothing to set here.
#
# ============================================================================
# Auth option 3 (FALLBACK): DeepSeek API key — bills PER TOKEN
# ============================================================================
# Switch to DeepSeek by setting this in config/temper.env:
#
#     TEMPER_AGENTS_AUTH=deepseek
#
# and providing the key in secrets/deepseek-api-key (see
# deepseek-api-key.example). The launch script reads that file; you usually do
# NOT need to set the key here. If you prefer an env override instead of the
# file, uncomment:
#
# TEMPER_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-your-deepseek-key
#
# ============================================================================
# Forgejo admin token (set by the launch script; do not paste a live one here)
# ============================================================================
# The launch script mints an admin token via the forgejo CLI and exports it to
# the provision step (TEMPER_FORGEJO_ADMIN_TOKEN) for that step only. You do
# not normally set it by hand.
#
# TEMPER_FORGEJO_ADMIN_TOKEN=
